       1	# Stage 2 Repair Design for the Edge-PML Obstruction
       2	
       3	Task: `task-stage2-repair-design`
       4	
       5	Predecessor facts:
       6	
       7	- `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-balance`
       8	- `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:edge-pml-linear-obstruction`
       9	- `fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:augmented-gronwall-energy`
      10	
      11	## Scope
      12	
      13	This artifact starts from the verified alpha \(=1\) source model obstruction and
      14	does not re-use that obstruction as final success.  It compares three repairs:
      15	
      16	1. a compatibility restriction on the old auxiliary data;
      17	2. a shifted-variable MPML-style damping of the free magnetic auxiliary mode;
      18	3. a covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye absorbing-layer model.
      19	
      20	The third model is the strongest fully closed result below: it has a positive
      21	monotone energy identity for arbitrary data in its variables.  It is a modified
      22	absorbing model, not algebraically identical to the old eight-variable unsplit
      23	PML formulation.
      24	
      25	Throughout this artifact
      26	\[
      27	\chi=\epsilon_0(\epsilon_s-\epsilon_\infty)>0,\qquad
      28	b_x=\frac{\sigma_x}{\epsilon_0},\quad b_y=\frac{\sigma_y}{\epsilon_0},
      29	\]
      30	and
      31	\[
      32	a_x=\frac{\sigma_y-\sigma_x}{\epsilon_0}=b_y-b_x,\qquad
      33	a_y=\frac{\sigma_x-\sigma_y}{\epsilon_0}=b_x-b_y.
      34	\]
      35	
      36	## Old-model obstruction term
      37	
      38	For the source equations the shifted magnetic variables
      39	\[
      40	M_x=Q_x-\mu a_xH_x,\qquad M_y=Q_y-\mu a_yH_y
      41	\]
      42	satisfy
      43	\[
      44	M_{x,t}=a_x\partial_yE-b_yM_x,\qquad
      45	M_{y,t}=-a_y\partial_xE-b_xM_y .
      46	\]
      47	In the \(x\)-edge case \(\sigma_x=s>0,\sigma_y=0\), the spatially constant
      48	mode with
      49	\[
      50	E=P=P_{z,1}=P_{z,2}=H_y=Q_y=0
      51	\]
      52	has \(M_x=Q_x+\mu b_xH_x\) conserved.  Hence
      53	\[
      54	H_x(t)=H_x(0)+\frac{M_x(0)}{\mu}t,\qquad
      55	Q_x(t)=Q_x(0)-b_xM_x(0)t .
      56	\]
      57	The obstruction is therefore the undamped shifted magnetic auxiliary \(M_x\) in
      58	the edge direction with zero transverse damping.  The \(y\)-edge case is
      59	symmetric with \(M_y\).
      60	
      61	## Repair 1: compatibility restriction on old auxiliaries
      62	
      63	The weakest repair is to restrict the old model to a physical auxiliary
      64	subspace that excludes the verified free mode.  In the constant \(x\)-edge
      65	case this means
      66	\[
      67	M_x(0)=Q_x(0)+\mu b_xH_x(0)=0
      68	\]
      69	for the spatially constant edge mode; in the constant \(y\)-edge case it means
      70	\[
      71	M_y(0)=Q_y(0)+\mu b_yH_y(0)=0 .
      72	\]
      73	This compatibility condition is physically meaningful if the old \(Q\)
      74	variables are interpreted as derived PML histories rather than independent
      75	initial data.
      76	
      77	The candidate energy for this restricted old model remains the positive
      78	augmented source energy
      79	\[
      80	\mathcal E_0(t)
      81	=\frac12\int_\Omega\left(
      82	\epsilon_0\epsilon_\infty E^2+\mu H_x^2+\mu H_y^2
      83	+\chi^{-1}P^2+P_{z,1}^2+P_{z,2}^2+Q_x^2+Q_y^2
      84	\right)\,dxdy .
      85	\]
      86	Under only bounded nonnegative absorptions, the previous verified result gives
      87	\[
      88	\mathcal E_0'(t)\le C_G\mathcal E_0(t).
      89	\]
      90	The compatibility condition removes the exact linear edge mode in the
      91	one-dimensional constant-mode test.  It does not by itself give a closed
      92	two-dimensional monotone energy, because in an \(x\)-edge
      93	\[
      94	M_{x,t}=-b_x\partial_yE
      95	\]
      96	when \(\sigma_y=0\).  Thus \(M_x=0\) is not invariant for general
      97	two-dimensional fields unless an additional transverse condition
      98	\(\partial_yE=0\) is imposed.  Classification: useful compatibility repair for
      99	the old edge free mode, but not a complete 2D monotone repair.
     100	
     101	## Repair 2: shifted-variable MPML damping
     102	
     103	The second repair keeps the shifted magnetic variables but adds a multi-axial
     104	or CFS-style damping \(\eta_x,\eta_y\ge0\) to the modes that were undamped at
     105	edges.  The modified \(Q\) equations are
     106	\[
     107	Q_{x,t}=-(b_x+\eta_x)Q_x+\mu(b_x+\eta_x)a_xH_x,
     108	\]
     109	\[
     110	Q_{y,t}=-(b_y+\eta_y)Q_y+\mu(b_y+\eta_y)a_yH_y,
     111	\]
     112	while the \(E,H,P,P_z\) equations are unchanged.  Equivalently,
     113	\[
     114	M_{x,t}=a_x\partial_yE-(b_y+\eta_x)M_x,
     115	\qquad
     116	M_{y,t}=-a_y\partial_xE-(b_x+\eta_y)M_y .
     117	\]
     118	Thus the old \(x\)-edge constant-mode obstruction becomes
     119	\[
     120	H_{x,t}=\frac{M_x}{\mu},\qquad M_{x,t}=-\eta_x M_x
     121	\]
     122	when \(E=0\), \(\sigma_x>0\), and \(\sigma_y=0\).  If \(\eta_x>0\), then for any
     123	constant \(c_x>0\)
     124	\[
     125	\mathcal E_{x,\eta}
     126	=\frac{\mu}{2}\left|H_x+\frac{M_x}{\mu\eta_x}\right|^2
     127	+\frac{c_x}{2}|M_x|^2
     128	\]
     129	is positive in \((H_x,M_x)\) and satisfies
     130	\[
     131	\frac{d}{dt}\mathcal E_{x,\eta}=-c_x\eta_x|M_x|^2\le0 .
     132	\]
     133	The \(y\)-edge formula is identical with \(x\) and \(y\) interchanged.
     134	
     135	This repair removes the specific linear-growth obstruction without imposing
     136	the compatibility \(M_i(0)=0\).  In the full two-dimensional system the energy
     137	derivative still contains transverse derivative couplings
     138	\[
     139	M_x\partial_yE,\qquad M_y\partial_xE,
     140	\]
     141	so a purely zeroth-order monotone energy is not closed by this shift alone.
     142	With derivative energies these terms are candidates for a dissipative
     143	lower-order or Gronwall estimate.  Classification: monotone for the isolated
     144	edge free subsystem, promising MPML repair for the old obstruction, but not a
     145	completed full 2D monotone proof in this artifact.
     146	
     147	## Repair 3: covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye absorbing layer
     148	
     149	The best closed repair is to replace the old independent \(P_z,Q\) auxiliary
     150	system by a covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye absorbing layer.  Let
     151	\(\rho_x,\rho_y\in L^\infty(\Omega)\) be nonnegative, time-independent layer
     152	profiles that vanish in the physical region, and put
     153	\[
     154	\rho=\rho_x+\rho_y,\qquad D_\rho=\partial_t+\rho .
     155	\]
     156	The modified model is
     157	\[
     158	\boxed{
     159	\begin{aligned}
     160	\epsilon_0\epsilon_\infty D_\rho E
     161	&=\partial_xH_y-\partial_yH_x-D_\rho P,\\
     162	\mu(\partial_t+\rho_y)H_x&=-\partial_yE,\\
     163	\mu(\partial_t+\rho_x)H_y&=\partial_xE,\\
     164	P+\tau D_\rho P&=\chi E .
     165	\end{aligned}}
     166	\]
     167	The boundary condition is the same PEC condition,
     168	\[
     169	E=0\quad\text{on }\partial\Omega .
     170	\]
     171	
     172	The model is local, agrees with the physical alpha \(=1\) Maxwell-Debye system
     173	where \(\rho_x=\rho_y=0\), and damps the electric polarization by the same
     174	covariant derivative used in the layer equation.  This last point is the
     175	essential repair of the old source-model term
     176	\(-((\sigma_x+\sigma_y)/\epsilon_0)EP\): the damping is applied to the
     177	Debye law itself, so the polarization contribution becomes positive
     178	dissipation rather than a sign-indefinite mixed product.
     179	
     180	### Candidate energy and positivity
     181	
     182	Use
     183	\[
     184	\mathcal E_\rho(t)
     185	=\frac12\int_\Omega\left(
     186	\epsilon_0\epsilon_\infty E^2+\mu H_x^2+\mu H_y^2+\chi^{-1}P^2
     187	\right)\,dxdy .
     188	\]
     189	This energy is positive definite in \((E,H_x,H_y,P)\) because
     190	\(\epsilon_0,\epsilon_\infty,\mu,\chi>0\).
     191	
     192	### Energy identity
     193	
     194	Multiplying the electric equation by \(E\), the magnetic equations by
     195	\(H_x,H_y\), integrating over \(\Omega\), and using \(E=0\) on
     196	\(\partial\Omega\) gives cancellation of the Maxwell principal boundary flux:
     197	\[
     198	\int_\Omega
     199	\left(E\partial_xH_y-E\partial_yH_x-H_x\partial_yE+H_y\partial_xE\right)
     200	\,dxdy=0 .
     201	\]
     202	The covariant polarization law gives
     203	\[
     204	E\,D_\rho P
     205	=\frac{1}{\chi}P\,D_\rho P+\frac{\tau}{\chi}|D_\rho P|^2
     206	=\frac{1}{2\chi}\partial_t(P^2)
     207	+\frac{\rho}{\chi}P^2
     208	+\frac{\tau}{\chi}|D_\rho P|^2 .
     209	\]
     210	Therefore
     211	\[
     212	\boxed{
     213	\frac{d}{dt}\mathcal E_\rho(t)
     214	=-\int_\Omega\left(
     215	\epsilon_0\epsilon_\infty\rho E^2
     216	+\mu\rho_yH_x^2
     217	+\mu\rho_xH_y^2
     218	+\frac{\rho}{\chi}P^2
     219	+\frac{\tau}{\chi}|D_\rho P|^2
     220	\right)\,dxdy\le0 .}
     221	\]
     222	
     223	Consequently
     224	\[
     225	\boxed{\mathcal E_\rho(t)\le \mathcal E_\rho(0)\quad\text{for all }t\ge0.}
     226	\]
     227	This is a genuinely monotone, long-time-uniform energy estimate.  It contains
     228	no independent \(P_{z,i}\) or \(Q_i\) variables, so the old edge free mode is
     229	not present.
     230	
     231	### Absorbing-layer status
     232	
     233	This repair should be viewed as a certified stable absorbing Maxwell-Debye
     234	layer.  It is PML-like in the sense that the layer profiles vanish in the
     235	physical region and the layer applies directional magnetic damping
     236	\(\rho_y,\rho_x\) together with covariant electric-polarization damping
     237	\(\rho=\rho_x+\rho_y\).  The proof above establishes stability and absorption
     238	through a monotone energy.  It does not prove exact perfect matching for every
     239	incidence angle; if exact reflectionless matching is required, a separate
     240	frequency-domain matching calculation remains open.
     241	
     242	## Selection
